a-b2d4-6a2a60540beb" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435806 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1,$ and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-1<\\frac{1}{y-x}<1 \\\\ y-x\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le 1,\\,y-x\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435805 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1069 "q-158565" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}.$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1072 #uuid "7303070a-5c11-542d-9464-8fd77a6c4c78" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435807 1074 "Notice that\n\n- $\\sqrt{x+y}$ is defined for $x$ and $y,$ such that $x+y\\ge 0,$ and\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡g(x,y)$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}$ is defined for values of $x$ and $y$ that satisfy $x+y\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y\\ge 0\\}.\n$$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435803 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1069 "q-158551" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{xy}.$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1072 #uuid "75318d12-00c4-544e-97a9-126ab4836587" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435808 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\nxy\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,xy\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435804 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1069 "q-158552" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+1}.$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1072 #uuid "f8d614db-1f17-5013-b1ed-45363a374722" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435809 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+1\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{3}\\ne -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{3}\\ne -1\\}.\n$$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435801 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1069 "q-158582" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1071 "Evaluate $z=\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}$ at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1072 #uuid "fb2bfb86-4e76-5321-aed7-06eaaf8188f8" 13194139534780 17592186045417 true] [17592186435810 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} \\\